  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Intercept on the move – two v two",
  "description": "An area of about 15 × 25 metres with a cone goal, about six metres wide, at each end. Two against two without goalkeepers. Score by dribbling the ball through the opponents' cone goal. With more players: play in pairs that swap every minute and a half, and let those resting fetch balls that go out.\n\nThe focus is the interception. Read the pass, step in ahead of the opponent and start the counter with the same touch – either a pass to the partner who has already started running, or a touch forward into space. A goal after an interception like that gives two points, other goals one.\n\nVariation: to make it pay even more, give three points when the interception and the pass to the partner were the same touch. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Stand so you can see both the ball and the player you want to intercept."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Go for the pass while it is travelling – not when it has already arrived."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Decide before the ball comes where it is going: to your partner or forward into space."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Your partner starts running as you step in, not after."
    }
  ],
